C Stack is authored for Clayton Kim.

Create Eval and Run Eval are portable adaptations of earlier skills in
theclaymethod/eval-creator-skill and theclaymethod/f-explainer.
Exact source paths, inspected revisions, and adaptations are in SOURCES.md.

Expert Mode and Distill Me adapt working-mode and retrospective review patterns
from Pstack by Lauren Tan, especially Poteto Mode, Automate Me, and Reflect.
Pstack: https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack
The upstream MIT license is preserved in licenses/pstack-MIT.txt.

Cross-Examine and its historical evaluation evidence originated in
https://github.com/theclaymethod/cross-examine.
Frozen evidence is retained as development provenance, not a current reliability claim.

The course skill adapts the teaching procedure of the Aili Bootcamp tutor
from Clayton Kim's personal site (teaching/skill-evals). The playground
exercises are the curriculum. The original hotel-analysis course is not
bundled. See SOURCES.md.

OpenAI Privacy Filter is referenced as an optional external dependency. Its
weights and source are not included; consult its own repository and model card
for licensing and usage details.

AI Evals Course's Evals Skills is referenced for established trace-analysis,
synthetic-input, review-interface, and evaluator workflows. Its skills and code
are not bundled here. See SOURCES.md for the inspected revision and links.
